// Model placement as a checked route condition (roadmap item 512,
// `docs/design/531-model-placement.md`).
//
// revl already routes runtime behaviour, and the route is checked rather than
// advised: `isolate <key> in realms(...)` names where a dependency resolves and
// the linker refuses a realm with no provider. This is the missing sibling for
// a MODEL call. A `model role` is a declared placement — a name plus where a
// call to it runs — and a `route model on <action>` block places one action's
// model calls by the origin class of what the action is given.
//
// The block is a PERMISSION checked at admission, not a scheduler: which of two
// admissible roles is cheaper is a policy question. The mechanical consequence
// is that it contributes NOTHING to the IR, so this file emits byte for byte
// what it would emit with the block deleted.
//
// Read the two arms together. `confidential -> local` is the only way a
// confidential input is placed at all, because `*` is DEFINED not to cover a
// confidentiality origin: `* -> cloud` covers `web`, `net`, `fs`, `input` and
// `model`, and it can never be the sentence that sends a confidential input off
// the device. `examples/rejections/gmodelplace_confidential_off_device.rvl` is
// the program one arrow away from this one that does not compile.
//
// This file is also the self-host's ADMITTING reproducer. The gate built from
// `selfhost/lower.rvl` refused every `route model` program at parse until slice
// 3 ported the construct; it now admits this one and refuses the rejection
// fixture beside it with the reference's own message.

model role local on_device
model role cloud off_device

service Answer {
  fn classify(text: Str) -> Str
  fn summarize(doc: Str) -> Str
}

component Classifier provides out: Answer {
  route model on classify {
    confidential -> local,
    * -> cloud
  }

  route model on summarize {
    confidential -> local
  }

  provide out {
    fn classify(text) = text
    fn summarize(doc) = doc
  }
}
